# Tracer: a value declaration that fails after one successful domain check.
#
# Before: the same statement rejected at -1 $in N, but retained only that
# final verification result. The earlier check and type-preflight scope were lost.
# have first, second, third N = 1, -1, 2
#
# Now: the same source retains all three value-formation checks, the proved
# 1 $in N, the failed -1 $in N, and the unchecked final membership.
# The whole declaration fails: no object or defining equality is published.
# Evidence: python3 examples/test_statements/run.py --leaf HaveObjEqualStmt
# Producer/consumer: tests/reading_failed_object_introductions.rs and
# src/reading/web/tests/failed-object-introductions.cjs.

have first, second, third N = 1, -1, 2
